<%# The card modal's heading, in display mode. Its own frame, distinct from the
    tile's (dom_id(card, :tile_title)) because the modal opens OVER the board and
    both are on the page at once — a shared id would have Turbo swapping the
    wrong one. See CardsController#title_context.

    A real <a> rather than a div with a click handler, so it's focusable and
    Enter-activatable for free. <a><h2>…</h2></a> is valid HTML. The negative
    margins let the hover surface extend slightly past the text without shifting
    the heading's position in the layout.

    NOTE: the id the dialog's aria-labelledby points at is deliberately NOT here
    — it lives on the wrapper OUTSIDE this frame (cards/show.html.erb), which
    survives the swap into edit mode.

    NO aria-label on the link, deliberately. It had one ("Edit card title") and
    that BROKE the dialog's accessible name: aria-labelledby computes the name
    from the wrapper's subtree, and a descendant's aria-label wins over its own
    text content — so the dialog announced as "Edit card title" instead of the
    card's title. Measured in the accessibility tree, not assumed. The link is
    not icon-only (it wraps the heading text), so it needs no label anyway: its
    name comes from that text, and `title` supplies the "you can rename this"
    hint as a description without touching either name. %>
<%= turbo_frame_tag dom_id(card, :modal_title) do %>
  <%= link_to edit_title_card_path(card, context: "modal"),
      class: "block -mx-2 -my-1 px-2 py-1 rounded-md no-underline text-inherit hover:bg-surface-200 transition-colors focus-visible:outline-none focus-visible:ring-2 focus-visible:ring-brand-700 focus-visible:ring-offset-1",
      title: "Rename card" do %>
    <h2 class="font-display text-xl font-bold text-ink-700 leading-tight"><%= card.title %></h2>
  <% end %>
<% end %>
